  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia Food Crisis 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A large-scale, climate-induced, humanitarian crisis has unfolded in the Horn of Africa, including Ethiopia where 6.8 million people are in urgent need of humanitarian assistance.&#xa0;
In March 2022, IFRC launched a Hunger Crisis Emergency Appeal in Ethiopia, to focus on the southern drought-affected regions (Somali, Oromia and SNNP), which were not supported in the Complex Crisis emergency appeal in northern Ethiopia. This Emergency Appeal is for 8M CHF and will support a total of 500,000 people affected by this climate-induced hunger crisis, with essential, lifesaving, humanitarian and early recovery support over 24 months (Livelihoods, Multipurpose cash, WASH, PGI).&#xa0;
BRC are looking to support IFRC&apos;s Emergency Appeal, provide surge delegates and look at longer term recovery programming with Netherlands RC in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </description>
